# CodeAlpha_ObjectDetectionTracking

Real-time **object detection and tracking** using YOLOv8 and ByteTrack. Built for the **CodeAlpha AI Internship – Task 4**.

## Features
- Input from **webcam** or **video file** (OpenCV)
- **YOLOv8** pre-trained on COCO (80 classes: person, car, dog, bottle, ...)
- **Object tracking** (ByteTrack, a SORT-family algorithm; BoT-SORT also available) so each object keeps a unique **ID**
- Bounding boxes with **class label, tracking ID and confidence**
- **Motion trails**, live **FPS**, per-class counts and total unique objects
- Filter by class (`--classes person car`), save output video, headless mode

## How it works
1. OpenCV reads each frame from the webcam/video.
2. `model.track(...)` runs YOLOv8 detection and associates detections across frames with the tracker (`persist=True` keeps IDs consistent).
3. Boxes, labels, IDs and trails are drawn on the frame and shown in real time.

## Setup
```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```
The YOLO weights (`yolov8n.pt`, ~6 MB) download automatically on the first run.

## Run
```bash
python main.py                                  # webcam
python main.py --source path/to/video.mp4       # video file
python main.py --source video.mp4 --save        # saves output/result.mp4
python main.py --classes person car --conf 0.4  # only people & cars
python main.py --model yolov8s.pt               # more accurate, slower
python main.py --tracker botsort.yaml           # different tracker
```
Press **q** in the window to quit. If you have no display (e.g. Google Colab), use `--no-show --save`.

## Options
| Option | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `--source` | `0` | `0` = webcam, or video path |
| `--model` | `yolov8n.pt` | `n/s/m/l/x` = faster → more accurate |
| `--tracker` | `bytetrack.yaml` | `bytetrack.yaml` or `botsort.yaml` |
| `--conf` | `0.35` | Detection confidence threshold |
| `--classes` | all | Track only these class names |
| `--trail` | `30` | Trail length in frames (0 = off) |
| `--speed` | `1.0` | Playback speed: `0.5` = half speed (slower), `2` = double |
| `--save` | off | Save annotated video |
| `--no-show` | off | No preview window |

## Tech stack
Python, OpenCV, Ultralytics YOLOv8, ByteTrack, NumPy
